WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.334 line:92%
-Our guest tonight was the mayor

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.235 size:84% position:42% line:92%
of South Bend, Indiana,

00:00:02.235 --> 00:00:03.269 line:92%
and a presidential candidate

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:04.270 line:92%
He's currently the United States

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:05.205 line:92%
secretary of Transportation.

00:00:05.205 --> 00:00:06.373 line:92%
Please welcome back to the sho

00:00:06.373 --> 00:00:07.807 line:92%
Secretary Pete Buttigieg.

00:00:07.807 --> 00:00:09.642 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hello!
How are you, Secretary?!

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:11.611 size:84% position:42%
-Hey, good to see you.
I'm doing well, thanks.

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:14.014 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I guess that's the first thin
I want to ask you,

00:00:14.014 --> 00:00:15.548 align:start size:94% position:6%
is how are you adjusting
to the new title?

00:00:15.548 --> 00:00:19.252 align:start size:94% position:6%
People knew you, obviously
as Mayor Pete for a long time.

00:00:19.252 --> 00:00:22.155 align:start size:94% position:6%
How is Secretary Buttigieg
fitting you?

00:00:22.155 --> 00:00:24.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, they say,
"Once a major, always a mayor,

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:27.394 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I'm always happy
to answer to "Mayor Pete,"

00:00:27.394 --> 00:00:30.296 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I'm certainly excited
to be the secretary.

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:32.499 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You got off to a sort of
inauspicious start,

00:00:32.499 --> 00:00:36.436 align:start size:94% position:6%
in that you had to quarantin
after being exposed.

00:00:36.436 --> 00:00:37.537 line:92%
How was quarantine for you

00:00:37.537 --> 00:00:41.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
Was it as difficult
as it's been for many people

00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:42.242 line:92%
-You know, I didn't love it,

00:00:42.242 --> 00:00:44.044 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I'm glad to be
on the other side of it.

00:00:44.044 --> 00:00:47.347
This morning, I took the dog
out for a walk before breakfas

00:00:47.347 --> 00:00:49.716
and it just felt,
even though it was gray and icy,

00:00:49.716 --> 00:00:52.118 size:81% position:41%
it felt fantastic just
to be outdoors again.

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:55.655
And, obviously, you know, we'r
urging people to be careful,

00:00:55.655 --> 00:00:58.058
to take every safety measure
and it was important to me

00:00:58.058 --> 00:01:00.460 align:start size:94% position:6%
to make sure we're
practicing what we preach.

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:02.829 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And so this was your firs
Oval Office meeting.

00:01:02.829 --> 00:01:04.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously, you couldn't
be there in person,

00:01:04.364 --> 00:01:06.299 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
-so you were wheeled in

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:07.634 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
on a big-screen TV.

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:09.669 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
How was that as an experience?

00:01:09.669 --> 00:01:12.572
-Yeah, I mean, you know,
like most Americans, right

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:15.809
I've always wondered what it's
like inside the Oval Office.

00:01:15.809 --> 00:01:18.678 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, the first time in my life
I'm actually invited

00:01:18.678 --> 00:01:20.980 align:start size:94% position:6%
to go into the Oval Office
for a meeting

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:24.184 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's in like
this disembodied form, right

00:01:24.184 --> 00:01:26.453 line:92%
Coming in on a TV cart by Zoom

00:01:26.453 --> 00:01:29.155 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, basically,
the most 2021 thing

00:01:29.155 --> 00:01:29.956 line:92%
that could possibly happen

00:01:29.956 --> 00:01:32.092
but it was a good meeting.
White House did a great jo

00:01:32.092 --> 00:01:34.194 size:81% position:41%
of making it possible
for me to participate.

00:01:34.194 --> 00:01:35.662 align:start size:94% position:6%
We were talking with senator
from both parties

00:01:35.662 --> 00:01:39.666 align:start size:94% position:6%
about how important it is
to build up our infrastructure

00:01:39.666 --> 00:01:40.834 line:92%
and I'm glad I could be there,

00:01:40.834 --> 00:01:42.936 align:start size:94% position:6%
even if it had to be
in that way.

00:01:42.936 --> 00:01:46.172
-You mentioned infrastructur
and the previous administratio

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:49.976 align:start size:94% position:6%
sort of was always promising
an infrastructure week

00:01:49.976 --> 00:01:50.777 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
that never came.

00:01:50.777 --> 00:01:52.178 line:92%
Based on that, I'm wondering

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:53.613 align:start size:94% position:6%
what was the state
of the department

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:55.915 align:start size:94% position:6%
or how are you finding
the state of the departmen

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:57.684 line:92%
in your early days of the job?

00:01:57.684 --> 00:02:01.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, the department ha
about 55,000 employees

00:02:01.254 --> 00:02:02.655 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they're
doing fantastic work,

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:06.359
but we do need to make sure that
we're actually putting our money

00:02:06.359 --> 00:02:07.660 align:start size:94% position:6%
where our mouth is
on infrastructure.

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:10.563
There's been a lot of talk
about it for years and years

00:02:10.563 --> 00:02:12.298 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now, we've actually got
to do something

00:02:12.298 --> 00:02:14.200 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I think we have
a chance to do it.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:16.369 size:75% position:38%
It's a huge priority
for President Biden.

00:02:16.369 --> 00:02:19.672
It's something most American
from both parties want us to d

00:02:19.672 --> 00:02:22.675
and we've just got to make sur
Washington actually responds

00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:26.045 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's a big part of what I feel
I'm here to do.

00:02:26.045 --> 00:02:28.748 align:start size:94% position:6%
-President Biden is proposin
billions of dollars

00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:31.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
in transportation aid
in this COVID relief package

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:35.522 align:start size:94% position:6%
Why is money for transportatio
so important,

00:02:35.522 --> 00:02:38.558 size:88% position:44% line:92%
in a time of a pandemic,

00:02:38.558 --> 00:02:39.826 align:start size:94% position:6%
where maybe people think
the money

00:02:39.826 --> 00:02:41.828 line:92%
could be better spent elsewhere?

00:02:41.828 --> 00:02:43.830 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right, so I think a lot
of people are asking,

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:46.432 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Why would you put transit
funding into a bill

00:02:46.432 --> 00:02:47.233 line:92%
that's about COVID relief?

00:02:47.233 --> 00:02:50.403
And let's be clear -- the reason
this bill is so urgent is

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:53.072 align:start size:94% position:6%
because it's about getting
relief to Americans.

00:02:53.072 --> 00:02:55.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's about getting shots
in arms.

00:02:55.041 --> 00:02:56.943 align:start size:94% position:6%
But transit and transportation
is part of that.

00:02:56.943 --> 00:02:59.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, how are people
supposed to get their shots,

00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:02.382 align:start size:94% position:6%
if transit agencies
around the country are

00:03:02.382 --> 00:03:03.583 size:88% position:44% line:92%
at risk of shutting down

00:03:03.583 --> 00:03:05.618 align:start size:94% position:6%
or cutting their routes
even further,

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:08.087 align:start size:94% position:6%
if they don't get immediat
financial relief?

00:03:08.087 --> 00:03:10.056 align:start size:94% position:6%
So this package really is
about the things

00:03:10.056 --> 00:03:13.126 align:start size:94% position:6%
that cannot wait,
that have to happen right away

00:03:13.126 --> 00:03:15.495 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's why
it's the top priority

00:03:15.495 --> 00:03:17.597 align:start size:94% position:6%
of the president
and the administration.

00:03:17.597 --> 00:03:21.067 size:75% position:38%
Look, most Americans
want this to happen,

00:03:21.067 --> 00:03:22.068 line:92%
Americans from both parties.

00:03:22.068 --> 00:03:25.138
We just got to make sure
Congress actually responds

00:03:25.138 --> 00:03:27.440 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think a lot of people
maybe fail to see

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:32.278 align:start size:94% position:6%
how transportation connect
to all different parts

00:03:32.278 --> 00:03:33.980 size:81% position:41% line:92%
of our political life.

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:36.883 align:start size:94% position:6%
One other thing it touches
is climate change.

00:03:36.883 --> 00:03:39.986 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you feel, in your position,
that there's a future

00:03:39.986 --> 00:03:41.487 align:start size:94% position:6%
for transportation
in this company, that maybe --

00:03:41.487 --> 00:03:45.425
in this country -- excuse me -
that maybe takes climate chang

00:03:45.425 --> 00:03:49.062 align:start size:94% position:6%
more into account
with what the future is?

00:03:49.062 --> 00:03:50.997 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Absolutely.
We have to.

00:03:50.997 --> 00:03:51.898 size:88% position:44% line:92%
There's no other choice.

00:03:51.898 --> 00:03:53.433 line:92%
Look, the biggest contributo

00:03:53.433 --> 00:03:56.402 align:start size:94% position:6%
of greenhouse gases
in the U.S. economy

00:03:56.402 --> 00:03:57.570 line:92%
is the transportation sector

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:59.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
But that means
the transportation sector

00:03:59.339 --> 00:04:02.308 align:start size:94% position:6%
could actually be the bigges
part of the solution,

00:04:02.308 --> 00:04:03.243 line:92%
and we're seeing that happen

00:04:03.243 --> 00:04:05.778 align:start size:94% position:6%
in every different form
of transportation.

00:04:05.778 --> 00:04:06.446 size:88% position:44% line:92%
We've got to support it.

00:04:06.446 --> 00:04:08.314 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, you look,
to take one example,

00:04:08.314 --> 00:04:09.983 size:78% position:39% line:92%
at electric vehicles.

00:04:09.983 --> 00:04:11.050 align:start size:94% position:6%
More and more,
we're seeing automakers,

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:15.321 align:start size:94% position:6%
including the classic longtime
automakers out of Detroit,

00:04:15.321 --> 00:04:17.123 size:78% position:39%
coming up with ideas
for electric vehicles

00:04:17.123 --> 00:04:19.559 align:start size:94% position:6%
and committing to them
and developing them

00:04:19.559 --> 00:04:21.194 line:92%
and selling them as we speak

00:04:21.194 --> 00:04:22.428 line:92%
Now, of course, simultaneously

00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:25.732 align:start size:94% position:6%
we've got to make sure not onl
that our cars are greener,

00:04:25.732 --> 00:04:27.934 align:start size:94% position:6%
but that people have
alternatives to driving,

00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:30.336 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we have
good subway systems,

00:04:30.336 --> 00:04:32.038 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we have good trains
in this country.

00:04:32.038 --> 00:04:35.074
I don't know why Americans
should be expected to settle

00:04:35.074 --> 00:04:37.577 align:start size:94% position:6%
for fewer options
for passenger rail

00:04:37.577 --> 00:04:42.181 align:start size:94% position:6%
than people who live in Chin
or Britain or Italy.

00:04:42.181 --> 00:04:44.117 size:84% position:42%
We should be the best
in all of these fields,

00:04:44.117 --> 00:04:48.121
and that's what we're callin
on Congress to help us do.

00:04:48.121 --> 00:04:50.556
-Be honest -- how excited
does the president get

00:04:50.556 --> 00:04:52.358 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you start talking
about trains?

00:04:52.358 --> 00:04:54.160 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like when high-speed rail
comes up,

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:56.896 align:start size:94% position:6%
is it a noticeable change
in his demeanor?

00:04:56.896 --> 00:05:00.566 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, you know, he famously
loves passenger rail,

00:05:00.566 --> 00:05:01.367 size:84% position:42% line:92%
so I thought I would be

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:03.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
the biggest passenger rail
enthusiast around,

00:05:03.369 --> 00:05:05.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I think
I'll be a close second,

00:05:05.171 --> 00:05:07.040 size:84% position:42%
but always second place
in this administration.

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:08.508 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's all over this.
And, again,

00:05:08.508 --> 00:05:11.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think, not just
as a personal fondness,

00:05:11.377 --> 00:05:13.212 align:start size:94% position:6%
but an understanding
that so many of the things

00:05:13.212 --> 00:05:14.781 align:start size:94% position:6%
this administration's
here to do.

00:05:14.781 --> 00:05:17.617 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yes, climate,
but also creating jobs,

00:05:17.617 --> 00:05:19.485 align:start size:94% position:6%
delivering equity
in this country.

00:05:19.485 --> 00:05:21.688 align:start size:94% position:6%
These are some of the things
that are at stake

00:05:21.688 --> 00:05:22.388 size:81% position:41% line:92%
in the choices we make

00:05:22.388 --> 00:05:25.658 align:start size:94% position:6%
about our trains, planes,
automobiles, ships, and more

00:05:25.658 --> 00:05:27.694 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Racial inequality
is something else

00:05:27.694 --> 00:05:29.962 align:start size:94% position:6%
that is affected,
you know, very much

00:05:29.962 --> 00:05:33.633 size:88% position:44%
by access to things like
public transportation.

00:05:33.633 --> 00:05:34.767 line:92%
Is that something that's sort of

00:05:34.767 --> 00:05:35.868 align:start size:94% position:6%
near the front of your lis
as well?

00:05:35.868 --> 00:05:37.170 align:start size:94% position:6%
Although, I am mentioning
a lot of things

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:39.772
that would be at the front
of your list, I understand

00:05:39.772 --> 00:05:42.208
-Yeah, but we've got to do
all these things at once -

00:05:42.208 --> 00:05:44.344 align:start size:94% position:6%
safety, climate, equity,
and jobs.

00:05:44.344 --> 00:05:45.745 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, yes,
when it comes to equity,

00:05:45.745 --> 00:05:47.580 align:start size:94% position:6%
racial equity
is a huge part of that.

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:49.849
Look, I know, when you're
thinking about, you know,

00:05:49.849 --> 00:05:52.852
racial justice in this country
Department of Transportation

00:05:52.852 --> 00:05:54.954 align:start size:94% position:6%
may not be the first thing
to pop into your mind,

00:05:54.954 --> 00:05:57.857 align:start size:94% position:6%
but think about the
Montgomery Bus Boycott.

00:05:57.857 --> 00:05:58.591 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Think about Rosa Parks.

00:05:58.591 --> 00:06:00.626 align:start size:94% position:6%
The history of civil right
in this country

00:06:00.626 --> 00:06:02.428 align:start size:94% position:6%
has always been
very closely tied

00:06:02.428 --> 00:06:05.498 align:start size:94% position:6%
to the question of equity
in transit and transportation.

00:06:05.498 --> 00:06:07.433 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's not just about,
you know, what neighborhoods

00:06:07.433 --> 00:06:10.803 align:start size:94% position:6%
get the subway stop or wha
communities get the investment

00:06:10.803 --> 00:06:13.139
but also the fact that, frankly,
in this country,

00:06:13.139 --> 00:06:15.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
we have a legacy
of investments happening

00:06:15.641 --> 00:06:17.810 align:start size:94% position:6%
at the expense
of communities of color.

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:19.479 align:start size:94% position:6%
So many Black neighborhoods,
for example,

00:06:19.479 --> 00:06:23.449 align:start size:94% position:6%
that were sometimes destroye
or literally cut in two

00:06:23.449 --> 00:06:25.918 size:75% position:38%
by a highway project
going through them.

00:06:25.918 --> 00:06:28.154 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's something that
has happened in this country

00:06:28.154 --> 00:06:31.391
and not just in the distan
past, but in very recent memory.

00:06:31.391 --> 00:06:34.160 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's something we could fi
and do something about,

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:37.697
if we have racial equity in mind
as we make the next set

00:06:37.697 --> 00:06:40.466 align:start size:94% position:6%
of transportation decision
for this country.

